// Extension → backend routing.
// Baked into the binary via include_str!.
// --backend CLI flag overrides.
// plugins: list of system plugin names to enable for this extension.
//          Defaults to ["prelude"] if not specified.
//
// 2026-08-03 (Phase 3, data-briev-config plan): migrated from targets.toml.
// Two key families in one flat .dbvl file:
//   - extension entries `<.ext>: <backend>; <defaults space-sep>; <plugins
//     space-sep>; <assembler>; <cross_verify_samples>;` — read by
//     TargetConfig::load. Optional trailing fields absent → defaults.
//   - tuning rows `target.<prefix>: <float_registers>; <dense_compute_density>;
//     <vector_min_width>; <isr_mechanism>; <frame_limit_bytes>;
//     <fp_reserved_temps>; <effect_carry_temp_min>;` — read by
//     config_tuning::load_target_settings.
// The .toml remains until both parity tests prove identical output.

.bv: llvm; --budget 256; prelude-native env print inline-frgn entry script execute-many; none; 50;
.ebv: electronics; ; prelude-electronics;
.sbv: circt; ; prelude-hw;
.rbv: webstack; --target wasm; prelude-web;
.abv: spirv; ; prelude execute-many;
// 2026-09-21 (bad-dialect plan): .bad — Briev Assembly Dialect. The
// target triple comes from --target (or host default); the backend lowers
// the portable core ISA through config/bad-isa.dbvl + bad-registers.dbvl.
.bad: bad; ; prelude;

// ── Per-target tuning (plan §8.1, frontend-driven-dispatch) ──────────
// Looked up by matching the compiler's target_triple PREFIX. Absent prefix →
// x86_64 defaults (below) + a compiler warning, so silent x86 assumptions never
// apply to unknown targets. Loaded by src/config_tuning.rs (TargetSettings).
//
//   float_registers      — register-pressure budget for vector-phi promotion
//                          (wasm = u32::MAX ≈ unlimited; the old code used
//                          usize::MAX, but TOML ints are i64 so u32::MAX keeps
//                          the "never fire" semantics).
//   dense_compute_density — cross-float-ops-per-field threshold for the
//                          #11 → #0 memory-attribute downgrade.
//   vector_min_width      — minimum isomorphic-group width for vector-phi
//                          promotion (below this the scalar-phi +
//                          extract/insert overhead exceeds the gain).
//   prefer_ebv            — 0/1 (2026-08-09, Phase 11): the preferred stdlib
//                          sibling variant for EXTENSIONLESS imports
//                          (SPEC §3.3). 1 → prefer `.ebv` (embedded /
//                          freestanding targets); 0 → prefer `.bv`. Absent →
//                          default 0.

// 2026-10-16 (absolute-limit addendum part 1): field 4 = frame_limit_bytes —
// the per-function frame ceiling the backend enforces (machine fact:
// displacement cliffs on hosted ISAs, declared RAM stack on embedded).
// 2026-10-21 (target-pressure effect shape): field 5 = fp_reserved_temps —
// FP registers reserved for the loop accumulator, expression temporaries, and
// effect-call arguments. Field 6 = effect_carry_temp_min — minimum
// temp-mediated Float fields for the carry shape.
// Defaults below are policy starting points, overridable per deployment.
target.x86_64: 16; 4.0; 4; 0; 2147483648; 4; 3; 2
target.aarch64: 32; 4.0; 4; 1; 2147483648; 4; 3; 2
target.arm64: 32; 4.0; 4; 1; 2147483648; 4; 3; 2
target.wasm32: 4294967295; 4.0; 4; 1; 1073741824; 4; 3; 2
target.wasm64: 4294967295; 4.0; 4; 1; 2147483648; 4; 3; 2
target.spirv64: 32; 4.0; 4; 1; 1073741824; 4; 3; 2
// 2026-09-14 (machine-entry plan): riscv64 bare metal (QEMU virt et al) —
// M-mode machine-timer/soft interrupts; field 4 names the ISR mechanism row
// (config/isr-targets.dbvl) that mechanism-less `node @ vector` declarations
// resolve through.
target.riscv64: 32; 4.0; 0; riscv_machine; 1048576; 4; 3; 2
// 2026-09-14 (rv64-finish plan Phase 5): ARM Cortex-M bare metal (QEMU MPS2 et al) —
// SysTick/NVIC interrupts; field 4 names the ISR mechanism row.
target.thumbv7m: 32; 4.0; 0; arm_cortex_m; 262144; 4; 3; 2
